-- title:
--   Four-layer locally closed subfunctor is representable
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a scheme. Suppose given the following data, functorial in affine points of $E$: (i) for every commutative ring $R$ and every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} R \to E$ an ideal $I_1(R,s) \subseteq R$, such that for every ring homomorphism $\psi : R \to R'$ one has $I_1(R', \operatorname{Spec}(\psi) \text{ followed by } s) = \psi_*(I_1(R,s))$, the ideal generated by the image; (ii) for every $s$ with $I_1(R,s) = 0$ a subset $U_2(R,s) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} R$, each assumed open, with $U_2(R', \operatorname{Spec}(\psi) \text{ followed by } s)$ equal to the preimage of $U_2(R,s)$ under the map of spectra induced by $\psi$; (iii) for every $s$ with $I_1(R,s) = 0$ and $U_2(R,s) = \operatorname{Spec} R$ an ideal $I_3(R,s) \subseteq R$, again transforming under $\psi$ by extension of ideals; (iv) for every such $s$ with moreover $I_3(R,s) = 0$ an open subset $U_4(R,s) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} R$, again transforming by preimage. (The data of each layer are indexed by the proofs of the vanishing or fullness conditions of the previous layers, and the compatibilities are required for all such proofs.) The conclusion asserts the existence of schemes $H$, $C_2$, $V_1$, $C_1$ and morphisms $j_4 : H \to C_2$, $j_3 : C_2 \to V_1$, $j_2 : V_1 \to C_1$, $j_1 : C_1 \to E$ with $j_4$ and $j_2$ open immersions and $j_3$ and $j_1$ closed immersions, such that for every commutative ring $R$ and every $s : \operatorname{Spec} R \to E$, the morphism $s$ factors through the composite $j_1 \circ j_2 \circ j_3 \circ j_4$ if and only if $I_1(R,s) = 0$, $U_2(R,s) = \operatorname{Spec} R$, $I_3(R,s) = 0$ and $U_4(R,s) = \operatorname{Spec} R$.
--
--   This is a representability criterion for a subfunctor of a scheme cut out by four successive conditions — closed, open, closed, open — on affine points, the representing object being obtained as an open subscheme of a closed subscheme of an open subscheme of a closed subscheme of $E$. It is used to produce the locally closed subscheme of a framed polarised abelian scheme parametrising embedded data, via the two single-layer criteria [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isClosedImmersion_forall_exists_comp_eq_iff_ideal_eq_bot`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isClosedImmersion_forall_exists_comp_eq_iff_ideal_eq_bot) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_opens_forall_range_subset_iff_eq_univ_of_forall_isOpen`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_opens_forall_range_subset_iff_eq_univ_of_forall_isOpen).
